{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc; sed -n '870,1110p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc; rg -n 'py/getattr|py/setattr|defn.*attr|:py/attrs|:py/type :instance' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc | head -55; rg --files src | rg '/cell'\"","aggregated_output":"(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.python.antlr.prelude/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.python.antlr.prelude\n  \"The Python runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §8.1, §8.2, §9.3). Python semantics for\n   operators, truthiness, equality, objects, exceptions and escapes live\n   here as guest code, not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications\n   of these names.\n\n   Value encoding:\n     int             host integer (untagged)\n     float           {:py/float x}: tagged on every host, because JS cannot\n                     tell 2 from 2.0 (owner decision 3); x is float64\n                     content (`data/float64`), never a bare host number,\n                     so 2.0 has one address on every host. Arithmetic\n                     unwraps with `data/float-value` and computes on bare\n                     host numbers. The prelude holds no integral float\n                     literal (JS reads 1.0 as 1), and no float literal\n                     reaches host arithmetic except through\n                     `data/float-value`, which also bridges a float64\n                     carrier decoded from a row back to a host number:\n                     1.0 is written (data/float-value 1)\n     bool            host true / false (numeric as 1 / 0)\n     None            :py/None\n     str             {:py/str \\\"...\\\"}\n     list            a cell holding {:py/type :list :items [...]}\n     dict            a cell holding {:py/type :dict :index {nkey slot}\n                     :keys [...] :vals [...]}: insertion order is the keys\n                     vector, never a host map's order; keys are normalized\n                     so 1, 1.0 and True are one key (see `py/key`)\n     set             a cell holding {:py/type :set :index {nkey slot}\n                     :keys [...]}: insertion order, keys normalized as for\n                     dicts\n     function        a cell holding {:py/type :function :name s :spec spec\n                     :defaults [...] :kwdefaults [[name v] ...]\n                     :code (fn [args] ...) :yang.call/entry\n                     (fn [invocation] ...)}; identity is the cell ref\n     class           a cell holding {:py/type :class :name s :base cls\n                     :attrs {name value}}\n     instance        a cell holding {:py/type :instance :class cls\n                     :attrs {name value}}\n     generator       a cell holding {:py/type :generator :name s :state st}\n                     and the slots of its state (see `py/gen-switch`)\n     iterator        a cell holding {:py/type :iterator :src s :i n}: what\n                     iter() makes of a sequence, advancing `py/iter-at` over\n                     src once per next; src None once exhausted\n     bound method    {:py/type :method :self obj :fn function}\n     tuple           {:py/type :tuple :items [...]}: a value; hashable when\n                     its elements are\n     slice           {:py/type :slice :start a :stop b :step c}\n     range           {:py/type :range :start a :stop b :step s}\n     module globals  a dict (owner decision 1): the module body receives it\n                     as `%globals` and every function closes over it, which\n                     is Python's own `__globals__`; a miss falls back to the\n                     builtins dict, and a miss there is NameError\n     module          a cell {:py/type :module :name s :dict d :body f}: the\n                     object `py/import` binds, its dict the module's own\n                     namespace, so attribute reads, writes and deletes are\n                     dict operations every function of the module sees, and\n                     `__dict__` reads the cell's dict; sys.modules itself is\n                     the dict `py.rt/modules`, `sys`, `builtins` and `importlib` the\n                     module objects `py/init!` pre-seeds into it; :body\n                     retains an imported module's image for reload\n\n   Calling convention: `py/call-kw` resolves Python methods and classes,\n   then discovers admitted entries through `yang.call`. Python function\n   entries bind positional arguments, keywords, defaults, `*args` and\n   `**kwargs` before applying their private `:code`; entryless builtins keep\n   their existing Python-local path.\n\n   Runtime state is allocated by `py/init!`, once per task, under the slot\n   `py.rt/state` (the literal `:py/uninit` until `py/init!` flips it to\n   `:py/ready` as its last write; a second call allocates nothing): the\n   four cells below, the builtin classes and functions as `py.b/*` keys,\n   and the builtins namespace dict `py.b/builtins`, which `py/global-get`\n   falls back to. All of it is reached through the store (`yin/def`\n   appears only in the prelude):\n     py.rt/ctx       the dynamic context, one record\n                     {:handlers :depth :base :frame}:\n                     :handlers  the handler stack: frames\n                                [kind payload rest n depth]; a :handler\n                                frame holds the continuation `raise`\n                                delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk every\n                                exit through it runs (raise passes the\n                                exception, escapes and normal completion\n                                pass None), a :generator frame the bottom\n                                of a running generator's own stack (raise\n                                passes it the exception); nil when empty\n                     :depth     the call depth within the current\n                                activation: the safepoint hook prelude\n                                counts it (RecursionError); the base\n         (if (= slot :py/missing) builtin (get (get c :vals) slot))))]\n    [py/class-ns-get\n     ;; a name assigned in a class body, read in that body: the class\n     ;; namespace as it is now, else `fallback` (globals, then builtins)\n     (fn [cls name fallback]\n       (let [x (get (get (cell/get cls) :attrs) name :py/missing)]\n         (if (= x :py/missing) (fallback) x)))]\n\n    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- functions\n    ;; A function's `spec` is static data from the lowering:\n    ;;   {:params [positional names] :star? bool :kwonly [names] :kwstar? bool}\n    ;; `defaults` holds the trailing positional defaults and `kwdefaults`\n    ;; [[name value] ...] the keyword-only ones, both evaluated at\n    ;; definition time. `code` takes one vector laid out as the parameters\n    ;; are written: positional, the *args tuple, keyword-only, the **kwargs\n    ;; dict.\n    [py/function-entry\n     ;; Generated boilerplate. Python functions are unbound here: a supplied\n     ;; receiver remains in the invocation but is not injected into args.\n     (fn [owner invocation]\n       (let [callee (get invocation :yang.call/callee :py/missing)\n             positional (get invocation :yang.call/positional :py/missing)\n             named (get invocation :yang.call/named :py/missing)\n             raise-exit (get invocation :yang.call/raise :py/missing)\n             binding-profile (get invocation :yang.call/binding-profile :py/missing)]\n         (if (if (= callee :py/missing) true\n                 (if (= positional :py/missing) true\n                     (if (= named :py/missing) true\n                         (if (= raise-exit :py/missing) true\n                             (not (= callee owner))))))\n           (raise-exit {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/invalid-invocation})\n           (if (not (= binding-profile :py/missing))\n             (raise-exit (assoc {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding}\n                                :yang.call/binding-profile binding-profile))\n             (let [fc (cell/get owner)\n                   result (cell/new :py/None)]\n               (py/try\n                 (fn []\n                   (cell/set! result\n                              ((get fc :code)\n                               (py/bind-args fc positional named))))\n                 (fn [e]\n                   ;; A retained generated exception forwards its original\n                   ;; condition unchanged (no new wrapper); a fresh source\n                   ;; exception still becomes the plain §8.10.7 thrown\n                   ;; condition. Retention rides the exception's identity,\n                   ;; outside source-writable attributes.\n                   (let [retained (py/retained-condition e)]\n                     (raise-exit\n                       (if (= retained :py/missing)\n                         (assoc {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown}\n                                :yang.call/value e)\n                         retained))))\n                 (fn [] (cell/get result))))))))]\n    [py/function-cell\n     (fn [name spec defaults kwdefaults code entry?]\n       (let [content (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :function)\n                                                        :name name)\n                                                 :spec spec)\n                                          :defaults defaults)\n                                   :kwdefaults kwdefaults)\n                            :code code)\n             f (cell/new content)]\n         (if entry?\n           (do (cell/set! f (assoc (cell/get f) :yang.call/entry\n                                   (fn [invocation]\n                                     (py/function-entry f invocation))))\n               f)\n           f)))]\n    [py/make-function\n     (fn [name spec defaults kwdefaults code]\n       (py/function-cell name spec defaults kwdefaults code true))]\n    [py/make-builtin-function\n     (fn [name spec defaults kwdefaults code]\n       (py/function-cell name spec defaults kwdefaults code false))]\n    [py/fn-error\n     (fn [fc msg] (py/type-error (py/str (data/str-concat (get fc :name) msg))))]\n    [py/index-of\n     (fn [xs x i]\n       (let [y (get xs i :py/stop)]\n         (if (= y :py/stop) -1 (if (= y x) i (py/index-of xs x (+ i 1))))))]\n    [py/pad\n     ;; the first n of xs, :py/missing where xs is shorter\n     (fn [xs n i acc]\n       (if (< i n) (py/pad xs n (+ i 1) (conj acc (get xs i :py/missing))) acc))]\n    [py/bind-keyword\n     ;; state is [positional-slots kwonly-slots kwargs-dict-or-nil]\n     (fn [fc state name x]\n       (let [spec (get fc :spec)\n             pi (py/index-of (get spec :params) name 0)\n             ki (py/index-of (get spec :kwonly) name 0)\n             dup (py/str (data/str-concat \"() got multiple values for argument '\"\n                                          name \"'\"))]\n         (if (< -1 pi)\n           (if (= (get (get state 0) pi) :py/missing)\n             (assoc state 0 (assoc (get state 0) pi x))\n             (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str)))\n           (if (< -1 ki)\n             (if (= (get (get state 1) ki) :py/missing)\n               (assoc state 1 (assoc (get state 1) ki x))\n               (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str)))\n             (if (nil? (get state 2))\n               (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n                                 \"() got an unexpected keyword argument '\" name \"'\"))\n               (if (py/dict-has? (get state 2) (py/str name))\n                 (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str))\n                 (do (py/dict-set (get state 2) (py/str name) x) state)))))))]\n    [py/bind-keywords\n     (fn [fc state kwargs i]\n       (let [pair (get kwargs i :py/stop)]\n         (if (= pair :py/stop)\n           state\n           (py/bind-keywords fc (py/bind-keyword fc state (get pair 0) (get pair 1))\n                             kwargs (+ i 1)))))]\n    [py/fill-defaults\n     (fn [fc slots defaults n i]\n       (if (< i n)\n         (if (= (get slots i) :py/missing)\n           (let [j (- i (- n (data/count defaults)))]\n             (if (< j 0)\n               (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n                                 \"() missing required positional argument '\"\n                                 (get (get (get fc :spec) :params) i) \"'\"))\n               (py/fill-defaults fc (assoc slots i (get defaults j)) defaults n\n                                 (+ i 1))))\n           (py/fill-defaults fc slots defaults n (+ i 1)))\n         slots))]\n    [py/lookup-pair\n     (fn [pairs name i]\n       (let [pair (get pairs i :py/stop)]\n         (if (= pair :py/stop)\n           :py/missing\n           (if (= (get pair 0) name) (get pair 1) (py/lookup-pair pairs name (+ i 1))))))]\n    [py/fill-kwdefaults\n     (fn [fc slots names i]\n       (let [nm (get names i :py/stop)]\n         (if (= nm :py/stop)\n           slots\n           (if (= (get slots i) :py/missing)\n             (let [d (py/lookup-pair (get fc :kwdefaults) nm 0)]\n               (if (= d :py/missing)\n                 (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n                                   \"() missing required keyword-only argument '\"\n                                   nm \"'\"))\n                 (py/fill-kwdefaults fc (assoc slots i d) names (+ i 1))))\n             (py/fill-kwdefaults fc slots names (+ i 1))))))]\n    [py/bind-args\n     ;; positional, then keywords, then defaults; every failure a TypeError\n     (fn [fc args kwargs]\n       (let [spec (get fc :spec)\n             n (data/count (get spec :params))\n             given (data/count args)\n             star (get spec :star?)]\n         (if (if (get spec :no-kw) (< 0 (data/count kwargs)) false)\n           (py/fn-error fc \"() takes no keyword arguments\")\n           (if (if (< n given) (not star) false)\n             (py/fn-error fc \"() takes too many positional arguments\")\n             (let [state (py/bind-keywords\n                           fc\n                           (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj [] (py/pad args n 0 []))\n                                               (py/pad [] (data/count (get spec :kwonly)) 0 []))\n                                     (if (get spec :kwstar?) (py/dict-new) nil))\n                           kwargs\n                           0)\n                   slots (py/fill-defaults fc (get state 0) (get fc :defaults) n 0)\n                   ko (py/fill-kwdefaults fc (get state 1) (get spec :kwonly) 0)\n                   with-star (if star\n                               (py/vconj slots\n                                         (py/tuple (if (< n given) (data/subvec args n) [])))\n                               slots)\n                   with-ko (data/into with-star ko)]\n               (if (get spec :kwstar?) (py/vconj with-ko (get state 2)) with-ko))))))]\n    [py/call (fn [f args] (py/call-kw f args []))]\n    [py/condition-exception\n     ;; Identity-owned provenance, separate from source-writable :attrs.\n     ;; Attribute edits and leaving the creating activation preserve it;\n     ;; reachability of the exception retains the entire condition/payload.\n     ;; Only this constructor writes the private slot, never a guest marker\n     ;; or a condition-shaped payload. No ambient identity registry is used.\n     (fn [cls msg condition]\n       (let [e (py/make-exc cls msg)]\n         (do (cell/set! e (assoc (cell/get e) :py/retained-condition condition))\n             e)))]\n    [py/retained-condition\n     ;; The identity-owned slot a generated exception carries, read without\n     ;; ever consulting source-writable :attrs; :py/missing when absent.\n     ;; A local instance only: a foreign or forged value has no slot.\n     (fn [e]\n       (if (= (py/content-type e) :instance)\n         (get (cell/get e) :py/retained-condition :py/missing)\n         :py/missing))]\n    [py/call-kw\n     (fn [f args kwargs]\n       (if (= (get f :py/type) :method)\n         (py/call-kw (get f :fn) (data/into (py/vconj [] (get f :self)) args) kwargs)\n         (if (= (py/content-type f) :class)\n           (py/instantiate f args kwargs)\n           (if (yang.call/eligible? f)\n             (yang.call/invoke\n               f args kwargs\n               (fn [condition]\n                 (if (= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)\n                   (let [value (get condition :yang.call/value)]\n                     (py/raise\n                       (if (if (= (py/content-type value) :instance)\n                             (py/subclass? (get (cell/get value) :class)\n                                           py.b/BaseException)\n                             false)\n                         value\n                         ;; A local hierarchy and fixed local message: neither\n                         ;; foreign class names nor foreign methods participate.\n                         (py/condition-exception\n                           (py/make-class \"ForeignException\" py.b/Exception)\n                           {:py/str \"foreign exception\"} condition))))\n                   (py/raise\n                     (py/condition-exception py.b/TypeError\n                                             {:py/str \"object is not callable\"}\n                                             condition)))))\n             (if (= (py/content-type f) :function)\n               (let [fc (cell/get f)]\n                 ((get fc :code) (py/bind-args fc args kwargs)))\n               (py/type-error {:py/str \"object is not callable\"}))))))]\n    [py/instantiate\n     (fn [cls args kwargs]\n       (let [inst (py/make-instance cls)\n             init (py/class-lookup cls \"__init__\")]\n         ;; without __init__ only exception classes take arguments (they\n         ;; become `args`); any other class takes none\n         (do (if (= init :py/missing)\n               (if (py/subclass? cls py.b/BaseException)\n                 ;; the builtin exception constructor takes positional\n                 ;; arguments only; an explicit __init__ binds keywords\n                 (if (< 0 (data/count kwargs))\n                   (py/type-error\n                     (py/str (data/str-concat (get (cell/get cls) :name)\n                                              \"() takes no keyword arguments\")))\n                   (py/setattr inst \"args\" (py/tuple args)))\n                 (if (if (< 0 (data/count args)) true (< 0 (data/count kwargs)))\n                   (py/type-error\n                     (py/str (data/str-concat (get (cell/get cls) :name)\n                                              \"() takes no arguments\")))\n39:     instance        a cell holding {:py/type :instance :class cls\n724:       (do (py/setattr cls \"__init__\"\n730:                             (do (py/setattr e \"args\" xs)\n731:                                 (py/setattr e \"value\" (get (get xs :items) 0 :py/None)))))))\n746:       (cell/new (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :instance) :class cls)\n751:         (do (py/setattr e \"args\" (py/tuple (py/vconj [] msg))) e)))]\n1106:                   (py/setattr inst \"args\" (py/tuple args)))\n1149:     ;; _PyObject_LookupAttr, the lookup py/getattr raises over and\n1211:    [py/getattr\n1215:    [py/setattr\n1226:               ;; the key is a call, as py/getattr's\n1513:         (do (py/setattr e \"args\"\n1819:                       (do (py/setattr e \"args\" (py/tuple [])) e)))\n2089:     ;; keys are calls, as py/getattr's\n3192:         (do (py/setattr e \"refusal\" r)\n3231:                     (do (py/setattr parent (get attr :py/str) m)\n3242:     ;; lookup py/getattr makes, else the sys.modules entry of\n3279:         (let [mn (py/getattr m \"__name__\")]\n3320:               (py/dict-set g n (py/getattr m (get n :py/str)))\n3553:  \"The function objects `py/getattr` and `py/gen-attr` hand out for a\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/resources/yin/vm/semantic/scanner-golden-c4.generate.clj; sed -n '1,180p' test/yang/call/conformance.clj; rg -n 'retained|forged|python' test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj | head -75; rg -n 'nohup|golden|deferred|abort|0 errors' collab/exception-track/*py* collab/yang-python/5c*\"","aggregated_output":";; Generator of the :c4/:py, :c4/:t and :c4/:pysp entries in\n;; test/yin/vm/semantic/scanner_goldens.cljc.\n;;\n;; Provenance: the JVM scanner answers of the C4 modules after the\n;; I4-a/I5/I6 prelude, lowering and reload moves — the deferred\n;; regeneration of the \"C4 scanner pins\" row in docs/agents/known-gaps.md\n;; (branch c4-i6-r4) — and after C4 I1 (aad451c5e, the hook prelude's\n;; appended require of py, which moved :pysp only). Run from the\n;; repository root on the JVM, with the\n;; test paths on the classpath, to rewrite the entries:\n;;\n;;   clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:t {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' -M:t \\\n;;    test/resources/yin/vm/semantic/scanner-golden-c4.generate.clj\n;;\n;; (not -M:test: that alias's main is the test runner and runs the suite)\n;;\n;; It rebuilds the module specs exactly as\n;; yin.vm.semantic.scan-test/c4-specs does, prints the live new-answer of\n;; the deferred groups (:py — the prelude module; :t — the reload test\n;; module; :pysp — the linked-safepoint test module), and rewrites their\n;; pins through the file's own\n;; generation pipeline: (pprint scanner-goldens) indented three columns\n;; under (def scanner-goldens '). Every other group — the six untouched\n;; :c4 modules plus :b0 and :register — is recomputed from the live\n;; scanners and checked against the committed pins first; a disagreement\n;; aborts before anything is written, because that would be a behavior\n;; change, not a pin move. Nothing is hand-authored and pprint is\n;; deterministic, so a rerun on an unchanged tree rewrites the same\n;; bytes. Rerun it (setting `deferred` to exactly the groups expected to\n;; move — a group left in the set has its movement absorbed silently)\n;; whenever the prelude, the safepoint, the lowering or the import\n;; programs move the scanner answers; yin.vm.semantic.scan-test fails\n;; until they are. Any slice touching those programs runs this generator\n;; in the same slice — a slice that moves the prelude without\n;; regenerating leaves the slow scan-test lane red on master.\n\n(require '[clojure.pprint :as pp]\n         '[clojure.string :as str]\n         '[yin.vm.semantic.corpus :as corpus]\n         '[yin.vm.semantic.scan-test :as scan-test]\n         '[yin.vm.semantic.scanner-goldens :as goldens])\n\n\n(def path \"test/yin/vm/semantic/scanner_goldens.cljc\")\n\n\n;; 2026-11-01: the yang-common-call adoption (6d6b7e711, \"link shared call\n;; runtime\") linked one shared runtime definition into every :c4 module, so\n;; each scanned module gained exactly +1 application with identical\n;; free-name sets (verified by the delta pass before this regeneration).\n;; The deferred set is therefore the six moved :c4 groups; :py/:pysp and\n;; :b0/:register did not move.\n(def deferred #{:py})\n\n\n(def specs (scan-test/c4-specs))\n\n\n(when (not= 8 (count specs))\n  (throw (ex-info \"c4-specs changed shape\" {:count (count specs)})))\n\n\n(def answers\n  (into {} (map (fn [[group spec]]\n                  [group (scan-test/new-answer (:ast spec))])\n                specs)))\n\n\n;; The gate: only the deferred groups may disagree with the committed\n;; pins. Anything else moving is a behavior change, not a pin move.\n(doseq [[group answer] answers\n        :when (and (not (deferred group))\n                   (not= answer (get-in goldens/scanner-goldens [:c4 group])))]\n  (throw (ex-info \"an untouched :c4 group moved\" {:group group})))\n\n\n(doseq [[group programs] [[:b0 scan-test/b0-programs] [:register corpus/programs]]\n        [n ast] programs\n        :when (not= (get-in goldens/scanner-goldens [group n])\n                    (scan-test/new-answer ast))]\n  (throw (ex-info \"a non-c4 golden moved\" {:group group :program n})))\n\n\n(doseq [group [:py :pysp :k :m :t :w :e :n]\n        :let [old (get-in goldens/scanner-goldens [:c4 group])\n              new (get answers group)\n              added (count (remove (set (:free-names old)) (:free-names new)))\n              removed (count (remove (set (:free-names new)) (:free-names old)))]]\n  (println (name group)\n           \":application-count\" (:application-count old) \"->\"\n           (:application-count new)\n           \":free-names\" (count (:free-names old)) \"->\" (count (:free-names new))\n           \"; added\" added \"removed\" removed \"free names\"))\n\n\n(doseq [group [:py :pysp :t]]\n  (println)\n  (println \"=== :c4\" (name group) \"new answer ===\")\n  (binding [*print-length* nil *print-level* nil]\n    (pp/pprint (get answers group))))\n\n\n(def intended\n  (reduce (fn [pins group] (assoc-in pins [:c4 group] (get answers group)))\n          goldens/scanner-goldens\n          deferred))\n\n\n(def def-form\n  (let [printed (str/trimr (with-out-str\n                             (binding [*print-length* nil *print-level* nil]\n                               (pp/pprint intended))))\n        [head & tail] (str/split-lines printed)]\n    (str \"(def scanner-goldens\\n  '\" head \"\\n\"\n         (str/join \"\\n\" (map #(str \"   \" %) tail)) \")\\n\")))\n\n\n(def rewritten\n  (let [original (slurp path)\n        marker \"(def scanner-goldens\\n\"\n        at (str/index-of original marker)]\n    (when (nil? at)\n      (throw (ex-info \"the golden def form moved\" {:path path})))\n    (str (subs original 0 at) def-form)))\n\n\n;; The rewrite must read back as exactly the intended pins.\n(let [anchor \"(def scanner-goldens\\n  '\"\n      at (str/index-of rewritten anchor)]\n  (when (or (nil? at)\n            (not= intended (read-string (subs rewritten (+ at (count anchor))))))\n    (throw (ex-info \"the rewrite does not read back as the intended pins\" {}))))\n\n\n(spit path rewritten)\n(println)\n(println \"wrote\" path)\n(ns yang.call.conformance\n  \"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\n   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\n   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\n\n   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\n   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\n   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\n   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`, `py/run-main`,\n   `clj/run-main`), reads each named export from the donor runtime's global\n   namespace, and projects it into the caller runtime's namespace under the\n   same name; then the caller source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own\n   entry. The composition is a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is\n   rewritten, no foreign `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is\n   inserted, and the projected value is the donor's own callable value\n   (identity survives).\n\n   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\n   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\n   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\n   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\n\n   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\n   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\n   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php`, `py` and `clj` are\n   published beside them. The AST walker is not a backend: its links are\n   refused until L-b.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.clojure :as clj-comp]\n    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\n    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n    [yang.core.names :as names]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-parser]\n    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as py-prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.render :as py-render]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn- publish-guest!\n  \"Publish guest module `spec` into the harness store, throwing immediately\n   with `result` in ex-data if publication is refused.\"\n  [spec]\n  (let [result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n    (when (= :refused (:status result))\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"Guest module publication refused: \" (or (:reason result) (:status result)))\n                      result)))\n    result))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-php\n  \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-py\n  \"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\n   `yang.call` revision.\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                   (:call-address @h/published)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-clj\n  \"`clj` published beside `js`, `php` and `py`, over the same host registry\n   and `yang.call` revision.\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (clj-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n\n\n(defn- parse-ok\n  \"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\"\n  [parse source]\n  (let [pk (parse source)]\n    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\n      (throw (ex-info \"donor or caller source does not parse\"\n                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\n    pk))\n\n\n(defn- python-export-symbol\n  [export]\n  (symbol (str \"xlang.python.export.\" export)))\n\n\n(defn- python-unit\n  [packet exports]\n  (u/lam [py-lower/globals-sym py-lower/globals-fn-sym]\n         (u/seq-nodes\n           (concat (map (fn [export]\n                          (u/sexp->uast\n                            (list 'py/global-set py-lower/globals-sym\n                                  {:py/str export} (python-export-symbol export))))\n                        exports)\n                   [(py-lower/lower-module-body packet)]))))\n\n\n(def frontends\n  \"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\n\n   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\n   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\n   - `:deps` (optional): pinned requirements beyond the runtime its\n     lowered units read directly (the clojure unit's `yang.call` reads);\n   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\n   - `:unit`: packet and projected exports to the lowered unit its\n     `:run-main` entry takes;\n   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\n     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP's named-function table, Python's main\n     module dictionary, the clojure runtime's task-local namespace cell);\n   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\n     the runtime's source resolves a called name;\n   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\"\n  {:typescript\n   {:runtime 'js,\n    :address #(:address @h/published),\n    :refusal [:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free],\n    :parse #(parse-ok ts-cst/parse-source %),\n    :unit (fn [packet _] (names/canonicalize (ts-lower/lower-unit packet))),\n    :run-main 'js/run-main,\n    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export})),\n    :project (fn [name value] (list 'js/define-global! name value)),\n    :render render/output},\n   :php\n   {:runtime 'php,\n    :address #(:address @published-php),\n    :refusal [:yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free],\n    :parse #(parse-ok php-cst/parse-source %),\n    :unit (fn [packet _] (u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body packet))),\n    :run-main 'php/run-main,\n    :read-export (fn [export]\n                   (list 'php/resolve-fn (str/lower-case export) export)),\n    :project (fn [name value]\n               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\n    :render php-h/render},\n   :python\n   {:runtime 'py,\n    :address #(:address @published-py),\n    :refusal [:yang.python.antlr/refusal :yang.python.antlr/undeclared-free],\n    :parse #(parse-ok py-parser/parse-source %),\n    :unit python-unit,\n    :run-main 'py/run-main,\n    :read-export (fn [export]\n                   (list 'py/global-get\n                         (list 'py/module-dict\n                               (list 'py/modules-ref {:py/str \"__main__\"}))\n                         {:py/str export})),\n    :project (fn [name value]\n               (list 'yin/def (list 'quote (python-export-symbol name)) value)),\n    :render py-render/output},\n   :clojure\n   {:runtime 'clj,\n    :address #(:address @published-clj),\n    :refusal [:yang.clojure/refusal :yang.clojure/undeclared-free],\n    :deps (fn [] {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published)}),\n    :parse clj-comp/read-forms,\n    :unit (fn [packet exports] (clj-comp/lower-unit packet exports)),\n    :run-main 'clj/run-main,\n    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'clj/global-get export)),\n    :project (fn [name value]\n               ;; The runtime global namespace is the one binding (as\n               ;; `js/define-global!` is for a JS caller): `lower-unit`\n               ;; reads each projected name through `clj/global-get`, so\n               ;; no task-store binding duplicates it. A caller top-level\n               ;; definition of the same name publishes after the\n               ;; projection and shadows it.\n20:  (delay (kit/publish-donor! :python contract/boundary-source)))\n42:  (let [target (read-export :python \"boundary_target\")]\n72:        retained 'probe.retained\n82:      [:python frontend]\n84:        (#{:fresh-named :fresh-closure :forged-retention} scenario)\n85:        (list 'let [original (list 'get (call (export (if (= scenario :forged-retention)\n86:                                                        \"forged\" \"payload\"))\n87:                                              (if (= scenario :forged-retention)\n93:                             :forged-retention (call (export \"raise_value\") [original]))]\n115:                (list 'let [retained (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])\n119:                               :retained (list '= (list 'get retained :route) :return))))\n134:        (#{:foreign-reception :retained-foreign-lifetime} scenario)\n141:                    retained (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])\n142:                    wrapper (list 'get retained :value)\n143:                    'probe.local (list 'if (list '= :return (list 'get retained :route))\n147:                    returned (list '= (list 'get retained :route) :return)]\n154:                                 :retained returned :local-foreign-exception local\ncollab/yang-python/5c-review-node-c4.log:38:0 failures, 0 errors.\ncollab/yang-python/5c-c4-final-jvm.log:41:0 failures, 0 errors.\ncollab/yang-python/5c-review-c4-jvm-slow.log:41:0 failures, 0 errors.\ncollab/exception-track/1794375661926-python-r2-kit-overlay-findings.md:76:No runtime, type builtin, shared prelude, or scanner golden changed. Scanner\ncollab/exception-track/1794375661926-python-r2-kit-overlay-findings.md:82:| Clean python-exception-test | 5 tests / 105 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors |\ncollab/exception-track/1794375661926-python-r2-kit-overlay-findings.md:83:| Shared four namespaces | 20 tests / 325 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors |\ncollab/exception-track/1794375661926-python-r2-kit-overlay-findings.md:84:| Same copied pin with archived acceptance prelude | 1 test / 4 assertions / 3 failures / 0 errors (expected red) |\ncollab/exception-track/1794375661926-python-r2-kit-overlay-findings.md:85:| Kondo, changed test namespace | 0 errors / 0 warnings |\ncollab/exception-track/1794375661926-python-r2-kit-overlay-findings.md:103:and detached with nohup.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
