             :clojure \\\"(def caught (cell/new 0))\\\\n\\\")\\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:92:                        :clojure \\\"(= (cell/get caught) 1)\\\"))\\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:97:                         :clojure \\\"(try (donor_raise) (catch Exception e (cell/set! caught (+ (cell/get caught) 1)) (throw e)))\\\")))\\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:127:                   :php \\\"$saved = null;\\\\n\\\" :clojure \\\"(def saved (cell/new nil))\\\\n\\\")\\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:133:                 :clojure \\\"(try (donor_raise) (catch Exception e (cell/set! saved e) e))\\\"))\\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:140:                          :php \\\"global $saved; throw $saved;\\\" :clojure \\\"(throw (cell/get saved))\\\")))\\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:147:                         :clojure \\\"(try (donor_raise) (catch Exception e (cell/set! cleaned (+ (cell/get cleaned) 1)) (throw e)))\\\")))))))\\ntest/yang/call/exception_source_test.clj:15:(deftest provenance-source-compilation-test\\ntest/yang/call/exception_r0_results.edn:117: :provenance [\\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:58:  (list 'cell/new\\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:135:        (list 'let [original (list 'cell/new {:foreign/payload :identity})\\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:158:        :else (throw (ex-info \\\"unknown provenance fixture\\\" {:scenario scenario}))))))\\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:64:         (do (yin/def (quote clj.rt/globals) (cell/new {}))\\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:72:       (do (cell/set! clj.rt/globals\\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:73:                      (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name value))\\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:77:       (if (data/contains? (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:78:         (get (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\\ndocs/design/datom.world.abi.md:78:names are historical provenance for the dissolved protocol, not names for a\\ncollab/exception-track/1794930000000-review-brief.md:8:1. **Correctness against the code**: verify the ruling's file:line claims (spot-check at least the load-bearing ones: js prelude.cljc:1581 and :1627; php prelude.cljc:190, :2264, :2384, :4217; python prelude.cljc:886-912, :1034; clojure.cljc:904, :1088, :1110, :1486). A wrong citation weakens a ruling of record — flag every miss.\\ncollab/exception-track/1794260000000-engineer-donor-link-absent-r3.prompt.md:49:- `clj -M:test -n yang.call.exception-contract-test -v yang.call.exception-contract-test/php-provenance-test`\\ncollab/exception-track/1794970001000-to-tsphp-your-js-and-php-rounds.md:17:The retained-condition provenance contract (Round 0, my seat — the contract + focused FAILING fixtures + kit exception-leg scaffolding on master before your rounds start) is the same for js and php, so the two rounds can share fixtures and design notes even though the rounds land separately.\\ncollab/exception-track/1794268000000-orchestrator-final-readiness-donor-link-absent.md:21:   problem statement's row list overstated: python→php and php-provenance\\ncollab/exception-track/1794260000000-engineer-donor-link-absent-r3.gemini-3.8-flash-high.stdout.log:2:{\\\"conversation_id\\\":\\\"ccc35339-416b-44a2-8e7a-771636b20152\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"response\\\":\\\"I have applied the uniform fail-fast hardening via `publish-guest!` across all runtime and donor publication sites in `conformance.clj`, and restructured the error paths in `conformance.clj`, `exception_legs.clj`, and `exception_probes.clj` so that publication refusals are caught during dereference and delivered as per-backend `:error` results.\\\\n\\\\nI have launched the first authorized verification test (`clojure-to-python-test`) and will wait for it to finish.\\\\n`clojure-to-python-test` completed with 9 failures / 0 errors (baseline-equal).\\\\nI have launched the second authorized test (`python-to-php-test`) and will wait for it to complete.\\\\n`python-to-php-test` completed with 6 failures / 18 errors (baseline-equal).\\\\nI have launched the third authorized test (`php-provenance-test`) and will wait for it to complete.\\\\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-09 20:02:57 GMT\\\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-10 03:02:57 +07\\\\n\\\\n# Round 3 Resolution: Universal Publication Hardening \\\\u0026 Per-Row Error Routing\\\\n\\\\n## 1. Summary of Actions\\\\n\\\\n1. **Finding 4 (Remaining Half) — Universal Fail-Fast Publication Hardening**:\\\\n   - Implemented a uniform private helper [`publish-guest!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L50-L60) in [`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj).\\\\n   - `publish-guest!` asserts `(when (= :refused (:status result)) (throw (ex-info ... result)))` immediately returning `result`.\\\\n   - Wired uniformly across all kit publication sites:\\\\n     - `published-php`\\\\n     - `published-py`\\\\n     - `published-clj`\\\\n     - `publish-donor!`\\\\n   - Prevents any guest module publication refusal from collapsing into a `nil` address.\\\\n\\\\n2. **Throw Reporting Path (P2 Resolution) — Per-Row Routing**:\\\\n   - In [`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj), introduced `error-results` mapping `Throwable` instances across all vector VM backends (`:register`, `:semantic`, `:stack`). Wrapped `run-exception-program`'s publication resolution and execution in `try ... (catch Throwable e (error-results e))`.\\\\n   - In [`test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj), wrapped `run-pair` and `run-leg` so that any `Throwable` thrown during donor dereference or execution is caught and delivered as `[id (kit/error-results e)]` across all scenario legs in the directed pair.\\\\n   - In [`test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj), wrapped `run-frontend` and `run-fixture` so that any `Throwable` thrown during `boundary-donor` dereference or execution is caught and delivered as `[id (kit/error-results e)]` across all fixtures of that frontend.\\\\n   - In `check-pair` and `check-frontend`, results enter the existing per-row loop:\\\\n     - `(instance? Throwable actual)` is `true` for all three backends.\\\\n     - `update-vals` captures `.getMessage` in `:host/error` and the complete refusal map in `:host/data`.\\\\n     - `:status` maps to `{:register :error, :semantic :error, :stack :error}`.\\\\n     - `do-report` logs individual per-backend operational failure errors for each row without aborting the `deftest`.\\\\n\\\\n3. **Correction Note on Round 2 Prose Mislabel**:\\\\n   - Appended a correction note in the findings document clarifying that the 13 canonical PHP provenance rows in `exception_r0_results.edn:34-46` are the 6 Red Failure rows (`:php/fresh-named`, `:php/fresh-closure`, `:php/binding`, `:php/protocol-not-callable`, `:php/saved-protocol-not-callable`, `:php/forged-retention`) and 7 Error rows (`:php/protocol-invalid-invocation`, `:php/protocol-unsupported-binding`, `:php/local-reception`, `:php/foreign-reception`, `:php/retained-foreign-lifetime`, `:php/saved-protocol-invalid-invocation`, `:php/saved-protocol-unsupported-binding`), matching the verified aggregate counts of 18 failures and 21 errors.\\\\n\\\\n4. **Authorized Verification Runs**:\\\\n   - `clojure-to-python-test`: Ran 1 tests containing 24 assertions. **9 failures, 0 errors** (baseline-equal).\\\\n   - `python-to-php-test`: Ran 1 tests containing 24 assertions. **6 failures, 18 errors** (baseline-equal).\\\\n   - `php-provenance-test`: Ran 1 tests containing 39 assertions. **18 failures, 21 errors** (baseline-equal).\\\\n\\\\n5. **Findings Document Updated**:\\\\n   - Appended the Round 3 section to [`collab/exception-track/1794241000000-engineer-donor-link-absent.gemini-3.8-flash-high.findings.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794241000000-engineer-donor-link-absent.gemini-3.8-flash-high.findings.md#L450).\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 2. Unified Diffs\\\\n\\\\n### `test/yang/call/conformance.clj`\\\\n```diff\\\\ndiff --git a/test/yang/call/conformance.clj b/test/yang/call/conformance.clj\\\\nindex 8cb2e908..a8bc2110 100644\\\\n--- a/test/yang/call/conformance.clj\\\\n+++ b/test/yang/call/conformance.clj\\\\n@@ -47,10 +47,21 @@\\\\n     [yin.vm :as vm]))\\\\n \\\\n \\\\n+(defn- publish-guest!\\\\n+  \\\\\\\"Publish guest module `spec` into the harness store, throwing immediately\\\\n+   with `result` in ex-data if publication is refused.\\\\\\\"\\\\n+  [spec]\\\\n+  (let [result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\\\\n+    (when (= :refused (:status result))\\\\n+      (throw (ex-info (str \\\\\\\"Guest module publication refused: \\\\\\\" (or (:reason result) (:status result)))\\\\n+                      result)))\\\\n+    result))\\\\n+\\\\n+\\\\n (def ^:private published-php\\\\n   \\\\\\\"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\\\\n    `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\\\\\\\"\\\\n-  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\\\\n+  (delay (publish-guest!\\\\n            (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\\\\n                                     (:call-address @h/published)))))\\\\n \\\\n@@ -58,7 +69,7 @@\\\\n (def ^:private published-py\\\\n   \\\\\\\"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\\\\n    `yang.call` revision.\\\\\\\"\\\\n-  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\\\\n+  (delay (publish-guest!\\\\n            (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\\\\n                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\\\\n \\\\n@@ -66,7 +77,7 @@\\\\n (def ^:private published-clj\\\\n   \\\\\\\"`clj` published beside `js`, `php` and `py`, over the same host registry\\\\n    and `yang.call` revision.\\\\\\\"\\\\n-  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\\\\n+  (delay (publish-guest!\\\\n            (clj-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\\\\n                                     (:call-address @h/published)))))\\\\n \\\\n@@ -187,6 +198,12 @@\\\\n   (clj-prelude/admit (php-prelude/admit (h/registry))))\\\\n \\\\n \\\\n+(defn- claims-call-sites?\\\\n+  \\\\\\\"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 call-site key anywhere.\\\\\\\"\\\\n+  [ast]\\\\n+  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\\\\n+\\\\n+\\\\n (defn publish-donor!\\\\n   \\\\\\\"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\\\\n    `xlang.donor.\\\\u003cfrontend\\\\u003e`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\\\\n@@ -196,17 +213,20 @@\\\\n   ([frontend source module]\\\\n    (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit deps]} (profile frontend)\\\\n          [refusal-key reason] refusal\\\\n+         ast (let [raw (core-module/module-tree\\\\n+                         [(core-module/require-node runtime)\\\\n+                          (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))])]\\\\n+               (cond-\\\\u003e raw\\\\n+                 (claims-call-sites? raw) u/annotate-call-sites))\\\\n          spec (core-module/module-spec\\\\n                 refusal-key reason (modules)\\\\n                 {:name module,\\\\n-                 :ast (core-module/module-tree\\\\n-                        [(core-module/require-node runtime)\\\\n-                         (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))]),\\\\n+                 :ast ast,\\\\n                  :exports '#{body},\\\\n                  :runtime-name runtime,\\\\n                  :runtime-address (address),\\\\n                  :deps (if deps (deps) {})})\\\\n-         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\\\\n+         result (publish-guest! spec)]\\\\n      {:frontend frontend,\\\\n       :module module,\\\\n       :address (:address result),\\\\n@@ -439,6 +459,12 @@\\\\n       #(excep