\t;; and a closure's failure ends the library function with the same outcome.\\\\\\\\n  2416\\\\\\\\t;;\\\\\\\\n  2417\\\\\\\\t;; What is derived, from the VM primitives and the `data` module only:\\\\\\\\n  2418\\\\\\\\t;; identity, inc/dec, second, the collection predicates (coll?/vector?/map?/\\\\\\\\n  2419\\\\\\\\t;; set?/seq?/list?/sequential?, from the `portable/*` adapters of data/count,\\\\\\\\n  2420\\\\\\\\t;; peek, dissoc and disj: a refusal as data says \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"not that kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), boolean?,\\\\\\\\n  2421\\\\\\\\t;; fn? (data/callable?), seq, rem, reverse, list, cons, vector, count,\\\\\\\\n  2422\\\\\\\\t;; contains?, rest, map/mapv/filter/remove/reduce (with reduced)/into/concat/merge,\\\\\\\\n  2423\\\\\\\\t;; keys/vals/disj and set union/difference,\\\\\\\\n  2424\\\\\\\\t;; comp, partial, gensym (explicit supply), not=, and `apply`, which is a\\\\\\\\n  2425\\\\\\\\t;; compiler intrinsic over the convention's argument vector.\\\\\\\\n  2426\\\\\\\\t;;\\\\\\\\n  2427\\\\\\\\t;; What stays a host primitive, named by the `kind` module: a symbol, a\\\\\\\\n  2428\\\\\\\\t;; keyword and a host string are distinguished or built only by the host\\\\\\\\n  2429\\\\\\\\t;; (symbol?, keyword?, name, symbol, keyword, str, int?), as is metadata access\\\\\\\\n  2430\\\\\\\\t;; (meta and with-meta). The current data ABI has no metadata-write export,\\\\\\\\n  2431\\\\\\\\t;; so with-meta is an explicit pure representation seam, not an ambient store.\\\\\\\\n  2432\\\\\\\\t;; No VM primitive tells a symbol from a keyword. Clojure Var identity is an\\\\\\\\n  2433\\\\\\\\t;; explicitly admitted kind/var? seam on the JVM; namespace lookup (resolve)\\\\\\\\n  2434\\\\\\\\t;; still requires a separately installed host capability.\\\\\\\\n  2435\\\\\\\\t;;\\\\\\\\n  2436\\\\\\\\t;; Known compromises: `reduced` is an untyped tagged map, so reduced? matches\\\\\\\\n  2437\\\\\\\\t;; any map holding :yin.k/reduced true; seq refuses a non-collection (a string\\\\\\\\n  2438\\\\\\\\t;; is the data module's str-* ops, not a seq); eager sequences are lists;\\\\\\\\n  2439\\\\\\\\t;; rem rejects non-integers and a zero divisor before arithmetic; the compiler\\\\\\\\n  2440\\\\\\\\t;; emits bare conj and vec, so a program may not define or bind either.\\\\\\\\n  2441\\\\\\\\t;; When collection calls are needed, invoke-value is a library helper whose\\\\\\\\n  2442\\\\\\\\t;; local capture is refused explicitly.\\\\\\\\n  2443\\\\\\\\t;;\\\\\\\\n  2444\\\\\\\\t;; Variadic Clojure functions are fixed-arity here (the convention has no\\\\\\\\n  2445\\\\\\\\t;; variadic parameter): str, list and vector admit 0 to 6 arguments, concat and\\\\\\\\n  2446\\\\\\\\t;; merge 0 to 4, union 0 to 6, difference 2, comp 0 to 3, partial binds 1 to 3.\\\\\\\\n  2447\\\\\\\\t;; A larger count is the\\\\\\\\n  2448\\\\\\\\t;; function's own arity error.\\\\\\\\n  2449\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2450\\\\\\\\t(def library-adapters\\\\\\\\n  2451\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The `:adapters` a program using `library` is compiled with: the data\\\\\\\\n  2452\\\\\\\\t   exports whose refusal the predicates read as data. The harness registers\\\\\\\\n  2453\\\\\\\\t   `portable/<name>` as `outcome-adapter` over the same `data/<name>`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  2454\\\\\\\\t  {'data/count 'portable/count\\\\\\\\n  2455\\\\\\\\t   'data/peek 'portable/peek\\\\\\\\n  2456\\\\\\\\t   'data/dissoc 'portable/dissoc\\\\\\\\n  2457\\\\\\\\t   'data/disj 'portable/disj\\\\\\\\n  2458\\\\\\\\t   'data/str-length 'portable/str-length})\\\\\\\\n  2459\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2460\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n  2461\\\\\\\\t(def kind-module\\\\\\\\n  2462\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The `kind` host module's exports, symbol to host function: the irreducible\\\\\\\\n  2463\\\\\\\\t   kind and name primitives (see the library notes). Every export is pure.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  2464\\\\\\\\t  (merge\\\\\\\\n  2465\\\\\\\\t    {'symbol? symbol?\\\\\\\\n  2466\\\\\\\\t     'keyword? key