r `:yang.call/thrown`. These reasons do not extend\\\\n  3864\\\\t`dao.stream`'s outcome algebra.\\\\n  3865\\\\t\\\\n  3866\\\\tThe receiving caller interprets an escaping exception as follows:\\\\n  3867\\\\t\\\\n  3868\\\\t1. A payload valid as an exception in its own runtime retains that\\\\n  3869\\\\t   runtime's ordinary catching and identity behavior.\\\\n  3870\\\\t2. A runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values, such as JavaScript,\\\\n  3871\\\\t   may deliver the original payload directly.\\\\n  3872\\\\t3. A runtime requiring exception objects, such as Python or PHP,\\\\n  3873\\\\t   represents an otherwise foreign payload with its own\\\\n  3874\\\\t   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\\\\n  3875\\\\t   payload. Catch-all catches this local object. Typed source catches\\\\n  3876\\\\t   match its local hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names.\\\\n  3877\\\\t\\\\n  3878\\\\t`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\\\\n  3879\\\\tUnchanged rethrow propagates the original condition without adding\\\\n  3880\\\\twrappers. Raising a new exception creates a new condition. Crossing back\\\\n  3881\\\\tinto a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original\\\\n  3882\\\\ttype and identity. Formatting a foreign payload must not implicitly\\\\n  3883\\\\tinvoke a foreign method.\\\\n  3884\\\\t\\\\n  3885\\\\tThe runtime associates its generated wrapper's identity with the retained\\\\n  3886\\\\tcondition for the wrapper's entire lifetime, separate from source-writable\\\\n  3887\\\\tattributes. The association normally lives in private wrapper-cell\\\\n  3888\\\\tcontents, or an equivalent task-owned identity structure with the same\\\\n  3889\\\\tlifetime. It survives storing or returning the wrapper after the creating\\\\n  3890\\\\tcall/catch activation has ended, and remains recoverable when that same\\\\n  3891\\\\twrapper is rethrown in another activation. Temporary catch state alone is\\\\n  3892\\\\tinsufficient. Reachability/reclamation must retain the condition and its\\\\n  3893\\\\tpayload while the wrapper is live, without an ambient registry.\\\\n  3894\\\\t\\\\n  3895\\\\tThe runtime must not detect wrappers or unwrap arbitrary maps by their\\\\n  3896\\\\tkey names. JavaScript may expose raw payloads for\\\\n  3897\\\\t`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\\\\n  3898\\\\tretain that failure's qualified condition. Rethrowing the same generated\\\\n  3899\\\\texception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\\\\n  3900\\\\tthrowing an unrelated value creates a new `:yang.call/thrown` condition.\\\\n  3901\\\\tSaved activation state refers to this identity-owned association; exiting\\\\n  3902\\\\tor restoring a catch does not destroy it.\\\\n  3903\\\\t\\\\n  3904\\\\tVM application/custody defects and host implementation failures remain\\\\n  3905\\\\toperational failures. Do not catch them broadly and relabel them as\\\\n  3906\\\\tsource exceptions. Existing explicit stream/module refusals keep their\\\\n  3907\\\\tsource mappings under the relevant profiles.\\\\n  3908\\\\t\\\\n  3909\\\\t#### 8.10.8 Cleanup, re-entry, and suspension\\\\n  3910\\\\t\\\\n  3911\\\\tEach activation establishes its own exception bridge and saves its\\\\n  3912\\\\tcallee runtime's dynamic context. Binding, body, and exit run under that\\\\n  3913\\\\tbridge. Before invoking the caller's raise exit, let source catches and\\\\n  3914\\\\tcleanup complete and restore saved handler/depth/frame state. Normal\\\\n  3915\\\\treturn restores it too. A source `finally` replacing a pending return\\\\n  3916\\\\tor exception does so before common propagation under its own rules.\\\\n  3917\\\\t\\\\n  3918\\\\tIn A-to-B-to-A calls, the innermost activation must not jump to an older\\\\n  3919\\\\tA handler past B. Its entry bridge is the boundary: inner A cleanup\\\\n  3920\\\\tprecedes B cleanup, which precedes outer A handling. Every activation\\\\n  3921\\\\towns its saved state and raise exit, without a single current-foreign-\\\\n  3922\\\\thandler cell or ambient dispatcher. Unchanged rethrow preserves the\\\\n  3923\\\\tinner exception as specified in section 8.10.7.\\\\n  3924\\\\t\\\\n  3925\\\\tCleanup runs once per actual exit. Resuming a suspended VM transition\\\\n  3926\\\\tmust not repeat parameter binding, argument evaluation, defaults,\\\\n  3927\\\\treference acquisition, or completed cleanup. The record, continuations,\\\\n  3928\\\\tand explicit runtime state use the existing continuation machinery and\\\\n  3929\\\\tits admission restrictions.\\\\n  3930\\\\t\\\\n  3931\\\\tA generator or asynchronous function returns its source-defined object.\\\\n  3932\\\\tSuspension on a stream effect keeps the activation; it is not a new\\\\n  3933\\\\tcall. A later generator resume or scheduled job has a new activation and\\\\n  3934\\\\tvalid bridge, never the raise exit of a call that already returned.\\\\n  3935\\\\tUnrestricted continuation escape across foreign frames is not implicitly\\\\n  3936\\\\tsupported: a claiming profile must define and test restoration and\\\\n  3937\\\\treference lifetimes for every crossed frame.\\\\n  3938\\\\t\\\\n  3939\\\\tInvoking a function-valued argument is internal Yin computation.\\\\n  3940\\\\tHost-initiated callbacks remain stream events under\\\\n  3941\\\\t`datom.world.abi.md`; this convention adds no host callback facility.\\\\n  4054\\\\t  writeback. Source-required side effects from evaluating arguments still\\\\n  4055\\\\t  occur; rejection must not erase them. Compatible profiles prove\\\\n  4056\\\\t  mutation, aliasing, cleanup, and suspension behavior.\\\\n  4057\\\\t- **Exceptions:** cover binding failures, arbitrary foreign thrown data,\\\\n  4058\\\\t  catch-all/typed catches, unchanged rethrow, replacement in `finally`,\\\\n  4059\\\\t  protocol-error rethrow, condition-shaped thrown maps, and A-to-B-to-A\\\\n  4060\\\\t  propagation. Assert original exception identity and cleanup order,\\\\n  4061\\\\t  not only rendered text. Store/return a generated `ForeignException`,\\\\n  4062\\\\t  finish its creating activation, then rethrow it from another activation\\\\n  4063\\\\t  and assert recovery of the original condition and payload identity.\\\\n  4064\\\\t- **Context lifetime:** repeated success/raise/success, cross-runtime\\\\n  4065\\\\t  recursion, and stream suspension/resume restore handler/depth/frame\\\\n  4066\\\\t  state and perform arguments/cleanup exactly once. Entry boilerplate\\\\n  4067\\\\t  must not double-count source recursion or tracing activations.\\\\n  4068\\\\t- **Publication/custody:** bundled/linked forms agree; two importing\\\\n  4069\\\\t  tasks have independent state. Existing gates still refuse foreign-task\\\\n  4070\\\\t  cells, forged refs, host functions, and inadmissible continuations.\\\\n  4071\\\\t- **Portability:** execute portable packet-to-UAST fixtures on JVM,\\\\n  4072\\\\t  Node, and Dart over the four VMs wherever existing contracts admit\\\\n  4073\\\\t  the program. JVM-only parsers may supply checked-in CST fixtures;\\\\n  4074\\\\t  parser availability is distinct from calling conformance.\\\\n  4075\\\\t\\\\n  4076\\\\tReport callable kinds, binding/value extensions, actual host/VM\\\\n  4077\\\\tcoverage as an explicit host-by-VM matrix, refusals, and remaining gaps\\\\n  4078\\\\tper frontend revision. A scalar example or common UAST grammar alone\\\\n  4079\\\\tdoes not establish conformance.\\\\n  4080\\\\t\\\\n  4081\\\\t#### 8.10.12 Cell-reference call routing and authenticity\\\\n  4082\\\\t\\\\n    18\\\\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\\\\n    19\\\\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\\\\n    20\\\\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\\\\n    21\\\\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\\\\n    22\\\\t\\\\n    23\\\\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\\\\n    24\\\\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\\\\n    25\\\\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php`, `py` and `clj` are\\\\n    26\\\\t   published beside them. The AST walker is not a backend: its links are\\\\n    27\\\\t   refused until L-b.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    28\\\\t  (:require\\\\n    29\\\\t    [clojure.string :as str]\\\\n    30\\\\t    [yang.clojure :as clj-comp]\\\\n    31\\\\t    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\\\\n    32\\\\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\\\\n   277\\\\t(defn run-program\\\\n   278\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`{backend value}` of `ast`, linked against `donor`, on each vector VM.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   279\\\\t  [donor ast]\\\\n   280\\\\t  (let [src (link-source donor)]\\\\n   281\\\\t    (into (sorted-map)\\\\n   282\\\\t          (map (fn [backend]\\\\n   283\\\\t                 [backend\\\\n   284\\\\t                  (vm/value (h/run-linked backend ast {:modules (modules),\\\\n   285\\\\t                                                       :link-source src}))]))\\\\n   286\\\\t          (keys h/backends))))\\\\n   287\\\\t\\\\n   288\\\\t\\\\n   289\\\\t(defn agreed\\\\n   290\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The one value every backend of `results` answered, else\\\\n   291\\\\t   `{:disagreement results}`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   292\\\\t  [results]\\\\n   293\\\\t  (let [vs (set (vals results))]\\\\n   294\\\\t    (if (= 1 (count vs)) (first vs) {:disagreement results})))\\\\n   295\\\\t\\\\n   296\\\\t\\\\n   297\\\\t(defn call\\\\n   298\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Publish the donor `[frontend source]`, compose its `exports` into the\\\\n   299\\\\t   caller `[frontend source]`, run it on each vector VM and answer the\\\\n   300\\\\t   caller's rendered value when every backend agrees (else\\\\n   301\\\\t   `{:disagreement {backend rendered}}`).\\\\\\\"\\\\n   302\\\\t  