\\"The pure query the cell-ref ruling of record added: does the heap\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:406:   heap+seal predicate `check-ref!` consults, as a boolean, so compiled\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:410:  (make-effect :cell/authentic? {:cell c}))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:415:  {'new new-cell, 'get get-cell, 'set! set-cell!, 'authentic? authentic-cell?})\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:421:  {'new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :effectful [1] #{:cell/new} :none)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:422:   'get (vm/primitive-profile 'get :effectful [1] #{:cell/get} :none)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:423:   'set! (vm/primitive-profile 'set! :effectful [2] #{:cell/set!} :none)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:424:   'authentic? (vm/primitive-profile 'authentic? :effectful [1]\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:425:                                     #{:cell/authentic?} :none)})\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:428:(defn register-cell-module\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:489:    \\\"This kernel's registers as heap-reclamation root values, each a whole\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:522:(defn- installing?\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:527:(defn- block-on\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:539:(defn- mint-link-id\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:548:(defn append-link-request\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:570:(defn- handle-require\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:654:(defn require-handler\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:660:(defn try-require-handler\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:666:(defn default-registry\\n# Review brief: the exception-track ruling (1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md)\\n\\nRead `collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md` and review it as specified for your seat below. Also read the baseline audit at `collab/yang-python/1794900000000-reviewer-exception-uniformity-audit.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log` (last agent message) — the ruling's R1-R5 and its file:line claims come from that audit, at HEAD e9a0b430.\\n\\nWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12. READ-ONLY — you edit nothing; the deliverable is your final message.\\n\\nReview for:\\n1. **Correctness against the code**: verify the ruling's file:line claims (spot-check at least the load-bearing ones: js prelude.cljc:1581 and :1627; php prelude.cljc:190, :2264, :2384, :4217; python prelude.cljc:886-912, :1034; clojure.cljc:904, :1088, :1110, :1486). A wrong citation weakens a ruling of record — flag every miss.\\n2. **Completeness**: does R1-R5 actually capture \\\"exceptions compile down to the same continuation\\\" everywhere? Is anything from the audit's divergence list missing? Is anything in the ruling OVERREACHING (a requirement the design or an owner invariant contradicts)?\\n3. **Testability**: can each of R1-R5 be pinned by a focused test? Is the acceptance gate (the conformance-kit exception legs) sufficient to declare the track done, or does it have a hole (e.g. pairs, VM coverage, the dart leg)?\\n4. **Sequencing risks**: the proposed order (R3 js/python, R1 php, R2 python/php, R4 clojure) — what breaks if done in that order? Any round that must precede another?\\n\\nVerdict format: ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH AMENDMENTS (list them) / REJECT (with reasons), then your findings.\\n(ns yang.python.antlr.prelude-parity-test\\n  \\\"The prelude's Python semantics on all four VMs and every host this runs\\n   on (JVM and Node): arithmetic with bools, float tagging, truthiness,\\n   cross-type equality, dict key normalization, numeric hash and integer\\n   `is` (C3 slice S2), ranges, and a run through\\n   `py/run-module` over the real cell and data modules whose printed output\\n   is rendered at the boundary.\\n\\n   C4 slice P1: `py/init!` is idempotent, the builtins dict is seeded from\\n   the tables and is what a global read falls back to, and a mutated entry\\n   never changes an interpreter-generated exception's class. Cross-module\\n   exception identity is not tested here: it needs two units sharing one\\n   task's prelude, which arrives with P2.\\\"\\n  (:require [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\\n            [yang.python.antlr.int-ops-test :as ops]\\n            [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\\n            [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]\\n            [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\\n\\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\\n            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\\n\\n\\n(defn- opts-under\\n  \\\"The composition over the real modules, `integer` under `limits`.\\\"\\n  [limits]\\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\\n   :primitives vm/primitives,\\n   :modules (-> (module/empty-registry)\\n                module/register-cell-module\\n                (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\\n                (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\\n                prelude/admit)})\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast\\n                        vm/ast-contract))\\n\\n\\n(defn- vm-runners-under\\n  \\\"Each VM's runner over the composition `opts`, answering the finished VM.\\\"\\n  [opts]\\n  {:ast-walker (fn [ast] (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)),\\n   :semantic (fn [ast]\\n               (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\\n                                          (vm/ast->datoms ast)))),\\n   :stack (fn [ast]\\n            (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\\n                      (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\\n                      (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))),\\n   :register (fn [ast]\\n               (vm/run\\n                 (rvm/create-vm\\n                   (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\\n                   (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))})\\n\\n\\n(defn- runners-under\\n  \\\"Each VM's runner over the composition `opts`.\\\"\\n  [opts]\\n  (into {}\\n        (map (fn [[k run]] [k (fn [ast] (vm/value (run ast)))]))\\n        (vm-runners-under opts)))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private runners\\n  (runners-under (opts-under {::integer/max-bits 100000,\\n                              ::integer/max-digits 4300})))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private small-runners\\n  \\\"Runners under limits a float key or hash breaches: 60 bits (2^-1074\\n   needs 1075, P = 2^61 - 1 needs 61) and 5 decimal digits.\\\"\\n  (runners-under (opts-under {::integer/max-bits 60,\\n                              ::integer/max-digits 5})))\\n\\n\\n(defn- run-with-prelude\\n  \\\"The value of `form` (prelude notation) after `prelude-ast`, on each\\n   of `runners` (default: the ordinary limits).\\\"\\n  ([prelude-ast form] (run-with-prelude runners prelude-ast form))\\n  ([runners prelude-ast form]\\n   (let [ast (u/mark-tails (u/then prelude-ast (u/sexp->uast form)))\\n         attempt (fn [run]\\n                   (try (run ast)\\n                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\\n                          [:thrown (ex-message e)])))]\\n     (into {} (map (fn [[k run]] [k (attempt run)])) runners))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- with-float64\\n  \\\"`form` with every `{:py/float x}` payload as float64 content, as the\\n   lowering and the prelude build it (on JS, Jing's carrier: a bare 1.0\\n   there is the integer 1).\\\"\\n  [form]\\n  (walk/postwalk (fn [x]\\n                   (if (and (map? x) (contains? x :py/float))\\n                     (update x :py/float data/float64)\\n                     x))\\n                 form))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private cases\\n  \\\"[form expected], evaluated as one vector on each VM.\\\"\\n  '[[(py/add 1 {:py/float 2.5}) {:py/float 3.5}]\\n    [(py/add true 1) 2]\\n    [(py/sub 5 true) 4]\\n    [(py/mul 3 4) 12]\\n    [(py/mul 3 {:py/float 1.5}) {:py/float 4.5}]\\n    [(py/truediv 7 2) {:py/float 3.5}]\\n    [(py/float? (py/truediv 4 2)) true]\\n    [(py/float? (py/add 2 2)) false]\\n    [(py/neg 3) -3]\\n    [(py/neg {:py/float 0.5}) {:py/float -0.5}]\\n    [(py/truthy 0) false]\\n    [(py/truthy {:py/float 0.0}) false]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git diff 4cfa609d..HEAD --stat && git show --format=fuller --stat d9a73150 && rg -n 'ceded|registry|Decision|continuation' collab/exception-track/*registry* collab/exception-track/*decision* 2>/dev/null && nl -ba test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj | sed -n '38,62p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git diff 4cfa609d..HEAD --stat && git show --format=fuller --stat d9a73150 && rg -n 'ceded|registry|Decision|continuation' collab/exception-track/*registry* collab/exception-track/*decision* 2>/dev/null && nl -ba test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj | sed -n '38,62p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\" ...1794375661926-python-r2-kit-overlay-findings.md | 125 +++++++++++++++++++++\\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc            |  52 ++++++++-\\n .../yin/vm/semantic/scanner-golden-c4.generate.clj |   2 +-\\n test/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj           | 108 ++++++++++++++++++\\n test/yin/vm/semantic/scanner_goldens.cljc          |  57 +++++++++-\\n 5 files changed, 334 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)\\ncommit d9a73150088c0ae8d31ca10dc07a325e2da0c03c\\nAuthor:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\\nAuthorDate: Wed Nov 11 06:29:44 2026 +0700\\nCommit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\\nCommitDate: Wed Nov 11 06:29:44 2026 +0700\\n\\n    python R2 reception: wrap foreign payloads in a generated ForeignException\\n    \\n    py/call-kw's thrown handler no longer raises an otherwise-foreign payload\\n    raw. A payload already valid as a local BaseException instance is delivered\\n    unchanged; an otherwise-foreign payload becomes a generated local\\n    ForeignException (base Exception) retaining the complete condition in a\\n    private :py/retained-condition slot (identity-owned, outside source-writable\\n    :attrs — R5). Adds py/condition-exception + py/retained-condition, and a\\n    minimal `type` builtin so the acceptance probe `type(e).__name__` can name\\n    the wrapper.\\n    \\n    Pin: yang.call.python-exception-test/python-foreign-reception-test\\n    (:python/local-reception stays green; :python/foreign-reception and the\\n    [:clojure :python :typed-catch] leg R→G; the rethrow pins land green with\\n    the egress unit).\\n    \\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc  | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\\n test/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n 2 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\\nzsh:1: no matches found: collab/exception-track/*registry*\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"status\":\"failed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files collab | rg 'exception.*(ced|surface|decision)|ced.*exception'\\nsed -n '1,180p' test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj\\nsed -n '372,412p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc\\nrg -n 'retained-condition|retained.*condition|ForeignException' docs/design/yang.antlr.md | head -25\\nsed -n '1,100p' src/cljc/yin/vm/cells.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_