:clojure \\\"(try (donor_raise) (catch Exception e (cell/set! cleaned (+ (cell/get cleaned) 1)) (throw e)))\\\")))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- call\\n  [frontend export args]\\n  (kit/boundary-call-form (kit/export-form frontend export)\\n                          (kit/observation-vector-form args) []))\\n\\n\\n(defn observation-form\\n  [{:keys [donor caller scenario probe-export]}]\\n  (let [result 'leg.result\\n        original 'leg.original\\n        transfer {:transferred (list '= :raise (list 'get result :route))\\n                  :once (list '= 1 (list 'get result :transfers))\\n                  :after (list 'get result :after)\\n                  :reason (list 'get (list 'get result :condition) :yang.call/reason)\\n                  :payload-identical\\n                  (list '= original (list 'get (list 'get result :condition) :yang.call/value))}\\n        probe-export (or probe-export \\\"probe\\\")\\n        simple {:returned (list '= :return (list 'get result :route))\\n                :value (list 'get result :value)}]\\n    (kit/guard-exceptions-form\\n      [donor caller]\\n      (case scenario\\n        (:catch-all :typed-catch :binding :success-raise-success)\\n        (list 'let [result (call caller probe-export [])] (kit/observation-map-form simple))\\n        :round-trip\\n        (list 'let [result (call donor \\\"home\\\" [(kit/export-form caller probe-export)\\n                                               (kit/export-form caller \\\"done\\\")])]\\n              (kit/observation-map-form simple))\\n        :retained-lifetime\\n        (list 'let [original (list 'get (call donor \\\"payload\\\" []) :value)\\n                    'leg.saved (call caller \\\"save_foreign\\\" [])\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; The `cell` module\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;;\\n;; A cell is a mutable location in the task's `:heap`, reached by a sealed\\n;; `:cell-ref` (Architect cell ruling, slice 1). These are pure effect\\n;; constructors like the stream module's: they touch no heap, and the engine\\n;; interprets the effects they return. The heap is VM state, so a mutation\\n;; is shared by every closure over the ref and is never rolled back when a\\n;; continuation is invoked (box semantics). Beside the three mutators the\\n;; module publishes `authentic?`, the ruling-of-record query a caller's\\n;; compiled code asks the issuer before dereferencing a cell-ref-shaped\\n;; callee; it answers a boolean and changes nothing.\\n\\n(defn new-cell\\n  [v]\\n  (make-effect :cell/new {:val v}))\\n\\n\\n(defn get-cell\\n  [c]\\n  (make-effect :cell/get {:cell c}))\\n\\n\\n(defn set-cell!\\n  [c v]\\n  (make-effect :cell/set! {:cell c, :val v}))\\n\\n\\n(defn authentic-cell?\\n  \\\"The pure query the cell-ref ruling of record added: does the heap\\n   issue `c` as a cell reference? The engine answers the same\\n   heap+seal predicate `check-ref!` consults, as a boolean, so compiled\\n   call routing can ask the issuer instead of guessing from a value's\\n   shape. Non-fatal, state unchanged.\\\"\\n  [c]\\n  (make-effect :cell/authentic? {:cell c}))\\n\\n\\n3874:   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\\n3878:`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\\n4061:  not only rendered text. Store/return a generated `ForeignException`,\\nsed: src/cljc/yin/vm/cells.cljc: No such file or directory\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"status\":\"failed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The unchanged-wrapper path appears sound: reception preserves an already-local exception, and egress forwards its retained condition. Attribute edits preserve the slot, and typed matching walks local class identities. I also found a scope change: the branch adds the Python-visible `type` builtin outside the ceded regions. The Clojure forgery prob