{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/resources/yin/vm/semantic/scanner-golden-c4.generate.clj; sed -n '1,100p' test/yin/vm/semantic/scanner_goldens.cljc; rg -n 'compose-exception|run-exception-program|guard-exceptions-form|boundary-call-form|observation' test/yang/call/conformance.clj; sed -n '1,155p' test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\"","aggregated_output":";; Generator of the :c4/:py, :c4/:t and :c4/:pysp entries in\n;; test/yin/vm/semantic/scanner_goldens.cljc.\n;;\n;; Provenance: the JVM scanner answers of the C4 modules after the\n;; I4-a/I5/I6 prelude, lowering and reload moves — the deferred\n;; regeneration of the \"C4 scanner pins\" row in docs/agents/known-gaps.md\n;; (branch c4-i6-r4) — and after C4 I1 (aad451c5e, the hook prelude's\n;; appended require of py, which moved :pysp only). Run from the\n;; repository root on the JVM, with the\n;; test paths on the classpath, to rewrite the entries:\n;;\n;;   clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:t {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' -M:t \\\n;;    test/resources/yin/vm/semantic/scanner-golden-c4.generate.clj\n;;\n;; (not -M:test: that alias's main is the test runner and runs the suite)\n;;\n;; It rebuilds the module specs exactly as\n;; yin.vm.semantic.scan-test/c4-specs does, prints the live new-answer of\n;; the deferred groups (:py — the prelude module; :t — the reload test\n;; module; :pysp — the linked-safepoint test module), and rewrites their\n;; pins through the file's own\n;; generation pipeline: (pprint scanner-goldens) indented three columns\n;; under (def scanner-goldens '). Every other group — the six untouched\n;; :c4 modules plus :b0 and :register — is recomputed from the live\n;; scanners and checked against the committed pins first; a disagreement\n;; aborts before anything is written, because that would be a behavior\n;; change, not a pin move. Nothing is hand-authored and pprint is\n;; deterministic, so a rerun on an unchanged tree rewrites the same\n;; bytes. Rerun it (setting `deferred` to exactly the groups expected to\n;; move — a group left in the set has its movement absorbed silently)\n;; whenever the prelude, the safepoint, the lowering or the import\n;; programs move the scanner answers; yin.vm.semantic.scan-test fails\n;; until they are. Any slice touching those programs runs this generator\n;; in the same slice — a slice that moves the prelude without\n;; regenerating leaves the slow scan-test lane red on master.\n\n(require '[clojure.pprint :as pp]\n         '[clojure.string :as str]\n         '[yin.vm.semantic.corpus :as corpus]\n         '[yin.vm.semantic.scan-test :as scan-test]\n         '[yin.vm.semantic.scanner-goldens :as goldens])\n\n\n(def path \"test/yin/vm/semantic/scanner_goldens.cljc\")\n\n\n;; 2026-11-01: the yang-common-call adoption (6d6b7e711, \"link shared call\n;; runtime\") linked one shared runtime definition into every :c4 module, so\n;; each scanned module gained exactly +1 application with identical\n;; free-name sets (verified by the delta pass before this regeneration).\n;; The deferred set is therefore the six moved :c4 groups; :py/:pysp and\n;; :b0/:register did not move.\n(def deferred #{:py})\n\n\n(def specs (scan-test/c4-specs))\n\n\n(when (not= 8 (count specs))\n  (throw (ex-info \"c4-specs changed shape\" {:count (count specs)})))\n\n\n(def answers\n  (into {} (map (fn [[group spec]]\n                  [group (scan-test/new-answer (:ast spec))])\n                specs)))\n\n\n;; The gate: only the deferred groups may disagree with the committed\n;; pins. Anything else moving is a behavior change, not a pin move.\n(doseq [[group answer] answers\n        :when (and (not (deferred group))\n                   (not= answer (get-in goldens/scanner-goldens [:c4 group])))]\n  (throw (ex-info \"an untouched :c4 group moved\" {:group group})))\n\n\n(doseq [[group programs] [[:b0 scan-test/b0-programs] [:register corpus/programs]]\n        [n ast] programs\n        :when (not= (get-in goldens/scanner-goldens [group n])\n                    (scan-test/new-answer ast))]\n  (throw (ex-info \"a non-c4 golden moved\" {:group group :program n})))\n\n\n(doseq [group [:py :pysp :k :m :t :w :e :n]\n        :let [old (get-in goldens/scanner-goldens [:c4 group])\n              new (get answers group)\n              added (count (remove (set (:free-names old)) (:free-names new)))\n              removed (count (remove (set (:free-names new)) (:free-names old)))]]\n  (println (name group)\n           \":application-count\" (:application-count old) \"->\"\n           (:application-count new)\n           \":free-names\" (count (:free-names old)) \"->\" (count (:free-names new))\n           \"; added\" added \"removed\" removed \"free names\"))\n\n\n(doseq [group [:py :pysp :t]]\n  (println)\n  (println \"=== :c4\" (name group) \"new answer ===\")\n  (binding [*print-length* nil *print-level* nil]\n    (pp/pprint (get answers group))))\n\n\n(def intended\n  (reduce (fn [pins group] (assoc-in pins [:c4 group] (get answers group)))\n          goldens/scanner-goldens\n          deferred))\n\n\n(def def-form\n  (let [printed (str/trimr (with-out-str\n                             (binding [*print-length* nil *print-level* nil]\n                               (pp/pprint intended))))\n        [head & tail] (str/split-lines printed)]\n    (str \"(def scanner-goldens\\n  '\" head \"\\n\"\n         (str/join \"\\n\" (map #(str \"   \" %) tail)) \")\\n\")))\n\n\n(def rewritten\n  (let [original (slurp path)\n        marker \"(def scanner-goldens\\n\"\n        at (str/index-of original marker)]\n    (when (nil? at)\n      (throw (ex-info \"the golden def form moved\" {:path path})))\n    (str (subs original 0 at) def-form)))\n\n\n;; The rewrite must read back as exactly the intended pins.\n(let [anchor \"(def scanner-goldens\\n  '\"\n      at (str/index-of rewritten anchor)]\n  (when (or (nil? at)\n            (not= intended (read-string (subs rewritten (+ at (count anchor))))))\n    (throw (ex-info \"the rewrite does not read back as the intended pins\" {}))))\n\n\n(spit path rewritten)\n(println)\n(println \"wrote\" path)\n(ns yin.vm.semantic.scanner-goldens\n  \"Historical v3 scanner answers generated on JVM from master 993d5411.\n   Only :c4/:py was regenerated after C4 I2/I3 on e6337294; reproduce with\n   collab/1792570000000-engineer-p7m-scan-golden.clj. Only :c4/:py and\n   :c4/:t were regenerated after C4 I4-a/I5/I6 (branch c4-i6-r4);\n   only :c4/:pysp was regenerated after C4 I1 (aad451c5e, the hook\n   prelude's appended require of py); only :c4/:py was regenerated by the\n   value-display slice (06065e42), and only :c4/:pysp by the s3 tracing\n   slice (the trace hooks of the hook prelude); reproduce with\n   test/resources/yin/vm/semantic/scanner-golden-c4.generate.clj.\n   Any slice touching the prelude, safepoint, lowering or import\n   programs runs the generator in the same slice.\")\n\n\n(def scanner-goldens\n  '{:b0\n    {\"stream make\"\n     {:free-names #{},\n      :occurrences [],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 0,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{},\n       :ffi-ops #{},\n       :parked-ids #{},\n       :effects #{:stream/make}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations []}},\n     \"literal int\"\n     {:free-names #{},\n      :occurrences [],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 0,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations []}},\n     \"equality false\"\n     {:free-names #{=},\n      :occurrences [[= false]],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 1,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations [[= false]]}},\n     \"if true branch\"\n     {:free-names #{<},\n      :occurrences [[< false]],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 1,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations [[< false]]}},\n     \"gensym\"\n     {:free-names #{},\n      :occurrences [],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 0,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations []}},\n     \"literal set\"\n     {:free-names #{},\n      :occurrences [],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 0,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations []}},\n     \"literal nil\"\n     {:free-names #{},\n      :occurrences [],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 0,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations []}},\n     \"literal map\"\n     {:free-names #{},\n      :occurrences [],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 0,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations []}},\n     \"literal string\"\n     {:free-names #{},\n      :occurrences [],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 0,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations []}},\n     \"if false branch\"\n     {:free-names #{<},\n      :occurrences [[< false]],\n      :definitions [],\n      :application-count 1,\n      :requirements\n      {:store-keys #{}, :ffi-ops #{}, :parked-ids #{}, :effects #{}},\n      :join {:status :ok, :obligations [[< false]]}},\n     \"arity-0 lambda\"\n337:(defn compose-exception\n339:   followed by an unlowered boundary observation form. The source bodies\n344:  ([donor exports caller-frontend caller-source observation]\n347:             (u/sexp->uast observation)))))\n350:(defn observation-map-form\n351:  \"Emit a map whose known observation values are guest expressions.\n353:   and symbols within it. Dynamic boundary observations use explicit assoc,\n359:(defn observation-vector-form\n366:(defn boundary-call-form\n373:   (boundary-call-form callee positional named nil))\n385:                                 (observation-map-form\n400:                                               (observation-map-form\n407:(defn guard-exceptions-form\n432:  \"Uniform observation of a runtime root's output. Preserve its exception\n434:   identity evidence; use boundary-call-form for that. Success-call renders\n458:      (run-program donor (compose-exception donor exports caller-frontend caller-source))\n468:(defn run-exception-program\n(ns yang.call.exception-probes\n  \"Boundary materialization of exception-contract/fixtures. Synthetic entries\n   occur ONLY for delivery of boundary-generated conditions; source pairs\n   live in exception-legs. Every receiver/rethrow body is parsed source.\"\n  (:require [yang.call.conformance :as kit]\n            [yang.call.exception-contract :as contract]))\n\n\n(defn- read-export\n  [frontend name]\n  (kit/export-form frontend name))\n\n\n(defn- call\n  [callee args]\n  (kit/boundary-call-form callee (kit/observation-vector-form args) []))\n\n\n(def ^:private boundary-donor\n  (delay (kit/publish-donor! :python contract/boundary-source)))\n\n\n(defn- transfer-summary\n  [result]\n  {:transferred (list '= (list 'get result :route) :raise)\n   :once (list '= 1 (list 'get result :transfers))\n   :after (list 'get result :after)})\n\n\n(defn- reason\n  [result]\n  (list 'get (list 'get result :condition) :yang.call/reason))\n\n\n(defn- payload\n  [result]\n  (list 'get (list 'get result :condition) :yang.call/value))\n\n\n(defn- protocol-condition\n  [reason]\n  (let [target (read-export :python \"boundary_target\")]\n    (list 'get\n          (case reason\n            :yang.call/not-callable (call {} [])\n            :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n            (kit/boundary-call-form target :malformed-positional [])\n            :yang.call/unsupported-binding\n            (kit/boundary-call-form target [] []\n                                    {:yang.call/binding-profile :contract/unsupported}))\n          :condition)))\n\n\n(defn- injected\n  [condition]\n  ;; This is a boundary delivery fixture, never counted as a real-source\n  ;; directed pair. The source receiver still uses its ordinary call helper.\n  (list 'cell/new\n        (list 'assoc {} :yang.call/entry\n              (list 'fn ['invocation]\n                    (list (list 'get 'invocation :yang.call/raise) condition)))))\n\n\n(defn observation-form\n  \"A fixture's guest-side assertions as plain booleans and qualified reasons.\n   Neither live payloads nor wrappers are rendered or ferried between tasks.\"\n  [{:keys [scenario frontend protocol-reason]}]\n  (let [export #(read-export frontend %)\n        result 'probe.result\n        original 'probe.original\n        condition 'probe.condition\n        retained 'probe.retained\n        wrapper 'probe.wrapper\n        fresh-summary (assoc (transfer-summary result)\n                             :reason (reason result)\n                             :payload-identical (list '= original (payload result)))\n        protocol-summary (assoc (transfer-summary result)\n                                :reason (reason result)\n                                :condition-identical\n                                (list '= condition (list 'get result :condition)))]\n    (kit/guard-exceptions-form\n      [:python frontend]\n      (cond\n        (#{:fresh-named :fresh-closure :forged-retention} scenario)\n        (list 'let [original (list 'get (call (export (if (= scenario :forged-retention)\n                                                        \"forged\" \"payload\"))\n                                              (if (= scenario :forged-retention)\n                                                [(protocol-condition :yang.call/not-callable)] [])) :value)\n                    result (case scenario\n                             :fresh-named (call (export \"donor_raise\") [])\n                             :fresh-closure\n                             (call (list 'get (call (export \"make_exploder\") []) :value) [])\n                             :forged-retention (call (export \"raise_value\") [original]))]\n              (kit/observation-map-form fresh-summary))\n\n        (= scenario :binding)\n        (list 'let [result (call (export \"needs_argument\") [])]\n              (kit/observation-map-form\n                (assoc (transfer-summary result) :reason (reason result))))\n\n        (#{:shape-return :shape-throw} scenario)\n        (list 'let [original {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\n                              :yang.call/data {:nested [:ordinary :data]}}\n                    result (call (export (if (= scenario :shape-return) \"echo\" \"raise_value\"))\n                                 [original])]\n              (kit/observation-map-form (if (= scenario :shape-return)\n                                          {:returned (list '= (list 'get result :route) :return)\n                                           :payload-identical (list '= original (list 'get result :value))}\n                                          fresh-summary)))\n\n        protocol-reason\n        (list 'let [condition (protocol-condition protocol-reason)\n                    'probe.injected (injected condition)]\n              (if (.startsWith (name scenario) \"saved-protocol-\")\n                (list 'let [retained (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])\n                            result (call (export \"later\") [])]\n                      (kit/observation-map-form\n                        (assoc protocol-summary\n                               :retained (list '= (list 'get retained :route) :return))))\n                (list 'let [result (call (export \"receive\") ['probe.injected])]\n                      (kit/observation-map-form protocol-summary))))\n\n        (= scenario :local-reception)\n        (list 'let [original (list 'get (call (export \"payload\") []) :value)\n                    condition (kit/observation-map-form\n                                {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n                                 :yang.call/value original})\n                    'probe.injected (injected condition)\n                    result (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])]\n              (kit/observation-map-form\n                {:returned (list '= :return (list 'get result :route))\n                 :payload-identical (list '= original (list 'get result :value))}))\n\n        (#{:foreign-reception :retained-foreign-lifetime} scenario)\n        (list 'let [original (list 'cell/new {:foreign/payload :identity})\n                    condition (kit/observation-map-form\n                                {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n                                 :yang.call/value original\n                                 :yang.call/data {:complete [:extra :evidence]}})\n                    'probe.injected (injected condition)\n                    retained (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])\n                    wrapper (list 'get retained :value)\n                    'probe.local (list 'if (list '= :return (list 'get retained :route))\n                                       (call (export \"is_foreign\") [wrapper])\n                                       {:value false})]\n              (let [local (list '= true (list 'get 'probe.local :value))\n                    returned (list '= (list 'get retained :route) :return)]\n                (if (= scenario :foreign-reception)\n                  (kit/observation-map-form\n                    {:returned returned :local-foreign-exception local})\n                  (list 'let [result (call (export \"later\") [])]\n                        (kit/observation-map-form\n                          (assoc (transfer-summary result)\n                                 :retained returned :local-foreign-exception local\n                                 :condition-identical (list '= condition (list 'get result :condition))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
