{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'authentic\\\\?|deftype Cell|defrecord Cell|cell/new|cell/get' src/cljc/yin src/clj/yin | head -90; sed -n '4110,4170p' src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc; sed -n '1205,1255p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc; tail -150 src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2456:;; `:heap`, as a pure `vm -> vm'`. The `:cell/new` arm counts allocations in\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2773:          :cell/new\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2779:          :cell/get\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2780:          (let [id (check-ref! state :cell/get :cell-ref (:cell effect))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2796:          :cell/authentic?\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:678:Runtime-allocated mutable locations are not AST nodes. They are the `cell` host module's `cell/new`, `cell/get`, `cell/set!` and `cell/authentic?`, ordinary applications whose effects the engine interprets on all four VMs. `cell/new` answers a sealed `{:type :cell-ref :id :cell-N :seal s}`; the content lives in the task's `:heap` (see `state.md`), never in the named store. `cell/authentic?` is the ruling-of-record pure query (yang.antlr.md 8.10.12): the heap's own yes-or-no on a candidate reference, answered as data where `cell/get` would fail closed.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:680:**Reclamation.** The heap is collected (Architect heap-reclamation design, slice 1; this supersedes the cell ruling's \"heap reclamation can wait\"). The `:cell/new` effect counts allocations, and when the count reaches the threshold it runs a deterministic, stop-the-world mark-sweep before allocating:\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:384:;; module publishes `authentic?`, the ruling-of-record query a caller's\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:390:  (make-effect :cell/new {:val v}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:395:  (make-effect :cell/get {:cell c}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:410:  (make-effect :cell/authentic? {:cell c}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:415:  {'new new-cell, 'get get-cell, 'set! set-cell!, 'authentic? authentic-cell?})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:421:  {'new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :effectful [1] #{:cell/new} :none)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:422:   'get (vm/primitive-profile 'get :effectful [1] #{:cell/get} :none)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:424:   'authentic? (vm/primitive-profile 'authentic? :effectful [1]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:425:                                     #{:cell/authentic?} :none)})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:121:**Purpose:** `:heap` holds the task's cells, the mutable locations `cell/new` allocates and a sealed `:cell-ref` reaches. It is VM state, not continuation state: a write is seen by every holder of the ref and survives continuation re-entry (box semantics). `:gc` is its collector's state. Both are declared record fields wherever a VM is a positional record, and both start empty in every constructor and `spawn-module` child.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:123:**Reclamation:** deterministic, allocation-triggered, stop-the-world mark-sweep, tracing kernel positions and value positions in two modes (`ast.md` Part 6),, a pure `vm -> vm'` (`yin.vm.engine/collect`). `:since` counts allocations; when it reaches `:threshold`, the `:cell/new` effect collects before allocating, and the threshold becomes `max(:base, 2 x live)`. `:base` is a composition parameter (`:gc-threshold`, default 4096). Marking runs over the heap as it was when the cycle began, and the sweep removes only ids of that snapshot, so an id allocated at or after the cycle's counter start is spared; a budgeted marker can later reuse it. `:pinned` holds cells whose refs left the VM's view on a stream or in an FFI request; they stay live for the task's life. Ids are never reused (`:id-counter` only grows), and a ref to a swept cell is refused with `:dead-or-forged-reference`. This supersedes the cell ruling's \"heap reclamation can wait\".\n                                  true))\n                (js/define-global! \"Symbol\" f)))\n         '(js/install-object!)\n         '(js/install-array!)\n         '(js/install-json!)\n         '(js/define-own! js.rt/global\n                          {:js/str \"undefined\"}\n                          (js/slot :js/undefined false false false))\n         '(js/define-own! js.rt/global\n                          {:js/str \"NaN\"}\n                          (js/slot (js/nan) false false false))\n         '(js/define-own! js.rt/global\n                          {:js/str \"Infinity\"}\n                          (js/slot (data/float64 (data/float-value ##Inf)) false false false))\n         '(js/define-global! \"globalThis\" js.rt/global)\n         '(let [c (js/make-object js.rt/obj-proto)]\n            (do (js/def-method! c \"log\" 0 js/console-log)\n                (js/define-global! \"console\" c)))]\n        ;; last, so a failed init never reports ready\n        [(define 'js.rt/state :js/ready) :js/undefined])\n      :js/undefined)))\n\n\n(def ^:private t4-definitions\n  [['js/args-object '(fn [args] (js/new-array args))]\n   ['js/spread-array-items\n    '(fn [items i out]\n       (if (< i (data/count items))\n         (js/spread-array-items\n           items\n           (+ i 1)\n           (js/vconj out (js/item-val (get items i))))\n         out))]\n   ['js/args-spread\n    '(fn [args value]\n       (if (js/array? value)\n         (data/into args\n                    (js/spread-array-items (get (cell/get value) :items) 0 []))\n         (js/throw-type-error {:js/str \"Spread value is not iterable\"})))]])\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order:\n   every prelude function, the literal state slot, then `js/init!`.\n   Defining them runs nothing.\"\n  (into (into (into (into (into (into core-definitions object-definitions)\n                                t4-definitions)\n                          array-definitions)\n                    json-definitions)\n              class-definitions)\n        [['js.rt/state :js/uninit] ['js/init! (init-form)]]))\n\n\n(def ^:private linked-definitions\n  \"The `js` module body; the common call runtime is pinned as a requirement.\"\n  definitions)\n\n\n(defn- definitions->uast\n  [defs]\n  ;; A linear `then` chain adds two tree levels per definition and can\n                               (py/method o py.b/gen-next)\n                               (if (= name \"__iter__\")\n                                 (py/method o py.b/gen-iter)\n                                 :py/missing))\n                             :py/missing))))))))))\n         :py/missing))]\n    [py/getattr\n     (fn [o name]\n       (let [x (py/lookup-attr o name)]\n         (if (= x :py/missing) (py/attr-error name) x)))]\n    [py/setattr\n     (fn [o name x]\n       (if (py/cell? o)\n         (let [c (cell/get o)\n               t (get c :py/type)]\n           (if (if (= t :instance) true (= t :class))\n             (do (cell/set! o (assoc c :attrs (assoc (get c :attrs) name x)))\n                 :py/None)\n             (if (= t :module)\n               ;; a module attribute is a binding in the module's dict\n               ;; (C4 I1), so the module's own functions see the write;\n               ;; the key is a call, as py/getattr's\n               (do (py/dict-set (get c :dict) (assoc {} :py/str name) x)\n                   :py/None)\n               (py/attr-error name))))\n         (py/attr-error name)))]\n\n    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- numbers\n    ;; Exact integer arithmetic goes through the module's guarded kernels.\n    [py/as-float\n     ;; The integer bridge can refuse before any host float operation.\n     (fn [a]\n       (if (py/float? a)\n         (py/num a)\n         (data/float-value (py/int-result (integer/to-float (py/num a))))))]\n    [py/arith\n     (fn [op a b]\n       (if (py/numeric? a)\n         (if (py/numeric? b)\n           (if (if (py/float? a) true (py/float? b))\n             (let [x (py/as-float a)\n                   y (py/as-float b)]\n               (py/float (if (= op :add) (+ x y)\n                             (if (= op :sub) (- x y) (* x y)))))\n             (let [x (py/num a)\n                   y (py/num b)]\n               (py/int-result\n                 (if (= op :add) (integer/add x y)\n                     (if (= op :sub) (integer/sub x y)\n                         (integer/mul x y))))))\n           (py/type-error {:py/str \"unsupported operand type\"}))\n                 :py/None])\n              :py/None)))\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order:\n   every prelude function, the literal state slot, then `py/init!`. Defining\n   them runs nothing.\"\n  (into core-definitions\n        [['py.rt/state :py/uninit]\n         ['py/init! (init-form)]]))\n\n\n(defn- definitions->uast\n  [defs]\n  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n\n\n(def functions-uast\n  \"The shared call runtime followed by every Python definition. Defining\n   them runs nothing, so this loads on any composition, with or without cells.\"\n  (definitions->uast (into call/definitions definitions)))\n\n\n(def uast\n  \"The bundled prelude: every definition, then the task's runtime state\n   allocated by `py/init!`.\"\n  (u/then functions-uast (u/sexp->uast '(py/init!))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter: the same definition list as the linker module `py`\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module the Python runtime profile is published as.\"\n  'py)\n\n\n(def runtime-keys\n  \"Every key `py/init!` allocates, the ready flag aside, sorted: the four\n   runtime cells, the builtin classes, functions and method\n   implementations, the builtins dict, and sys.modules with its three\n   pre-seeded module objects. Read from the same tables `init-form` reads.\"\n  (vec (sort-by str\n                (concat '[py.rt/ctx py.rt/limit py.rt/out py.rt/value py.b/builtins\n                          py.rt/modules py.rt/sys py.rt/builtins-mod py.rt/importlib]\n                        (mapv second builtin-classes)\n                        (mapv second builtin-functions)\n                        (mapv first method-implementations)))))\n\n\n(defn strip\n  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `py`; any other value as it\n   is. `py.b/*` and `py.rt/*` stay qualified: they are internal store keys,\n   and stripping them would collide (`py/list` and `py.b/list`).\"\n  [sym]\n  (core/strip \"py\" sym))\n\n\n(def ^:private module-definitions\n  \"The module's definition list: a `:py/uninit` placeholder for every\n   runtime key, so each read of one is discharged by an unconditional\n   module-level definition, then every definition, stripped.\"\n  (core/module-definitions \"py\" :py/uninit runtime-keys definitions))\n\n\n(def module-uast\n  \"The module tree: one application whose operands are the definitions,\n   in order, followed by `require yang.call`, applied to a lambda that\n   returns nil. Every definition runs on the main sequence before the\n   require, so the linker's scanners discharge every body read of a sibling\n   or runtime key. Defining runs nothing.\"\n  (core/module-tree module-definitions\n                    [(u/sexp->uast '(require (quote yang.call)))]))\n\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"The module's exports: every `py/` key of the definition list,\n   stripped. The runtime keys and the state slot are internal.\"\n  (core/exports \"py\" definitions))\n\n\n(def free-names\n  \"Every variable name some occurrence of the map AST reads unbound by an\n   enclosing lambda.\"\n  core/free-names)\n\n\n(def defined-keys\n  \"Every literal key the map AST defines with `yin/def`, at any depth.\"\n  core/defined-keys)\n\n\n(def ^:private module-free-names\n  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the\n   primitives and the host exports its manifest must declare.\"\n  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `py`\n   over the host registry `registry`. Every free name of the module tree\n   is declared under `:primitives`; a free name nothing supplies is\n   refused before anything is published. This namespace emits; it never\n   publishes.\"\n  [registry call-address]\n  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name,\n                     :ast module-uast,\n                     :exports module-exports,\n                     :requires {'yang.call call-address},\n                     :free-names module-free-names,\n                     :skip? #(= \"yang.call\" (namespace %)),\n                     :registry registry,\n                     :message \"the py module reads an undeclared name\",\n                     :refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"}))\n\n\n(def min-integer-bits\n  \"The smallest `::integer/max-bits` this profile admits: every inline\n   literal (up to 2^53 - 1) must fit (C3 S2).\"\n  53)\n\n\n(defn register-integer-module\n  \"Return `registry` with the `integer` module installed under `limits`\n   for this profile: refused when `::integer/max-bits` is under\n   `min-integer-bits`, otherwise `integer/register-integer-module`.\"\n  [registry limits]\n  (let [b (::integer/max-bits limits)]\n    (when-not (and (int? b) (<= min-integer-bits b))\n      (throw (ex-info \"the Python profile needs integer max-bits >= 53\"\n                      {:yang.python.antlr/refusal :yang.python.antlr/max-bits,\n                       ::integer/max-bits b}))))\n  (integer/register-integer-module registry limits))\n\n\n(defn admit\n  \"Return `registry` when it supplies every one of `host-names`, else\n   refuse it before any program runs, naming each missing export in\n   `:yang.python.antlr/missing`: a version-3 `integer` module (no\n   `float-digits`, `decimal->float`, `max-digits`) or a `data` module\n   registered without `:yin.vm.data/max-items` is a profile mismatch, not a\n   failure of the program that first calls the export. A Python\n   composition calls this after its registrars. Linking replaces it with\n   requirement discovery (yang.antlr.md 8.5.4).\"\n  [registry]\n  (core/admit registry host-names\n              \"the composition lacks host names the prelude calls\"\n              \"yang.python.antlr\"))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
